selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#course-overview\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Course overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#course-overview\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Combinatorics begins with a simple questions: How many ways can we arrange a collection of objects? Can a schedule, pairing, or design be made at all? What changes when two arrangements should count as the same? These questions show up in mathematics, computer science, probability, and more\u2026</p><p>We will learn foundational combinatorial techniques, the inclusion-exclusion principle, allowing us to count efficiently.</p>", "a[href=\"resources.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#resources\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h1><p>I will provide lecture notes or detailed references for all the topics we cover and you should know.</p><p>I may also include <em>additional material</em> like links to youtube videos and more. This additional material is <em>optional</em> and provided as an alternative explanation of the topics I cover.</p>", "a[href=\"#inclement-weather-and-emergencies\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Inclement weather and emergencies<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#inclement-weather-and-emergencies\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>We will follow University closure and inclement-weather decisions. If a closure prevents an exam, I will announce a new date through Blackboard and the course website. Please do not travel when conditions are unsafe.</p>", "a[href=\"lecture-notes/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Lecture Notes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#lecture-notes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h1><h2>Unit map<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#unit-map\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#id1\"]": "<table class=\"table\" id=\"id1\">\n<caption><span class=\"caption-text\">Course Contents</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id1\" title=\"Link to this table\">#</a></caption>\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><th class=\"head\"><p>Unit</p></th>\n<th class=\"head text-left\"><p>Main capability</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p>Enumeration and inclusion-exclusion</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>Define discrete objects precisely and count them using case structure, bijections, double counting, and overlapping restrictions.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p>Generating-function foundations</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>Encode sequences as formal power series and interpret algebraic operations as counting operations.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td><p>Recurrence models</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>Select states and initial conditions, derive and solve recurrences, and compare recursive, memoized, and bottom-up evaluation.</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td><p>Further topics</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>TBA</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>", "a[href=\"#weekly-hand-in-homework\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Weekly hand-in homework<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#weekly-hand-in-homework\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>A typical assignment has several problems and may involve computation, modeling, and proofs or other mathematical arguments. Please submit it online as a PDF (a handwritten, scanned PDF is welcome), make sure it is legible and labels each problem, explain your method as well as your final answer, and write complete mathematical statements. Please follow the deadline listed on the assignment page.</p><p>If you need more time, talk to me <strong>in advance of the deadline</strong> so we can work out an extension. We will deal with unforeseen emergencies on a case by case basis.</p>", "a[href=\"#id2\"]": "<table class=\"table\" id=\"id2\">\n<caption><span class=\"caption-text\">Grade weights breakdown</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id2\" title=\"Link to this table\">#</a></caption>\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><th class=\"head text-left\"><p>Component</p></th>\n<th class=\"head text-left\"><p>Weight</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p>Written hand-in homework</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>20%</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p>Online questions</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>15%</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p>Exam 1</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>16%</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p>Exam 2</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>16%</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p>Exam 3</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>16%</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p>Exam 4</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>16%</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-even\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p>Course check-in completion</p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p>1%</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"row-odd\"><td class=\"text-left\"><p><strong>Total</strong></p></td>\n<td class=\"text-left\"><p><strong>100%</strong></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>", "a[href=\"#materials\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Materials<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#materials\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>My <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"lecture-notes/index.html\"><span class=\"std std-doc\">lecture notes</span></a> are our main guide through the course. They may also link to explanatory videos or other freely available sources.</p><p>The principal reference is Keller and Trotter, <em>Applied Combinatorics</em>: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://appliedcombinatorics.org/book/app-comb-2.html\">Web edition</a> <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://appliedcombinatorics.org/book-pdf/app-comb-2017.pdf\">PDF edition</a></p>", "a[href=\"#academic-integrity\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Academic integrity<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#academic-integrity\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>We all share responsibility for creating a course environment built on honest work and learning. Please follow the <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://honesty.uark.edu/policy/\">University of Arkansas Academic Integrity Policy</a>; suspected violations are handled through the University process. You can find the specific expectations for collaboration and the use of artificial intelligence on the <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"assignments/index.html\"><span class=\"std std-doc\">assignments page</span></a>.</p>", "a[href=\"#unit-exams\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Unit exams<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#unit-exams\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>There are four unit exams: three in-class exams and one during the first part of the final-exam period.</p><p>Every exam problem will be parallel to an assigned homework problem in its required method and main solution steps, though the parameters, objects, or wording may change.</p>", "a[href=\"#syllabus\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Syllabus<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#syllabus\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h1><h2>Course overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#course-overview\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Combinatorics begins with a simple questions: How many ways can we arrange a collection of objects? Can a schedule, pairing, or design be made at all? What changes when two arrangements should count as the same? These questions show up in mathematics, computer science, probability, and more\u2026</p><p>We will learn foundational combinatorial techniques, the inclusion-exclusion principle, allowing us to count efficiently.</p>", "a[href=\"#course-organization\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Course organization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#course-organization\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>In class, I will introduce new topics and talk through their applications with you.</p><p>After most meetings, online questions provide a quick review of basic skills; they are graded automatically, and most allow multiple attempts.</p>", "a[href=\"#religious-observances-university-activities-and-other-excusable-conflicts\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Religious observances, University activities, and other excusable conflicts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#religious-observances-university-activities-and-other-excusable-conflicts\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>Please email me as early as you can about religious observances, required University activities, military service, jury duty, documented illness, a family crisis, or another excusable conflict. For an exam conflict you can anticipate, letting me know at least one week ahead is especially helpful. We will follow the applicable University policies and deadlines.</p><p>If you have three or more final exams on one day, you may be able to reschedule one under <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://policies.uark.edu/academic/150020.php\">Academic Policy 1500.20</a>. If it involves this course, please make your request before the Registrar\u2019s withdrawal deadline.</p>", "a[href=\"#learning-outcomes\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Learning Outcomes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#learning-outcomes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>By the end of the course, you should be able to:</p>", "a[href=\"#assessment\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Assessment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#assessment\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Course check-ins are brief questions I create to learn what is working for you in the course organization, pacing, and resources.</p><p><strong>Dropped assignments:</strong></p>", "a[href=\"#online-questions\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Online questions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#online-questions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>Online questions normally follow a lecture and are due by the start of our next class meeting. They focus on comfort with key vocabulary and formulas.</p>", "a[href=\"#communication-records-and-course-changes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Communication, records, and course changes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#communication-records-and-course-changes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Email is the best way to reach me with an individual question.</p><p>I will post course-wide announcements, grades, and updates in Blackboard, so please check your University email and Blackboard regularly.</p>", "a[href=\"#other-information\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Other information<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#other-information\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><h3>Accessibility and accommodations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#accessibility-and-accommodations\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>If you have approved accommodations, please request your accommodation letter and contact me early so we can make arrangements in time.\nIf you think you may need accommodations but have not yet set them up, the <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://cea.uark.edu/\">Center for Educational Access</a> can help. Temporary conditions can affect access too, so please reach out promptly when they arise.</p>", "a[href=\"#student-support\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Student support<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#student-support\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>Additional links are collected on the <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"resources.html\"><span class=\"std std-doc\">resources page</span></a>.</p>", "a[href=\"#accessibility-and-accommodations\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Accessibility and accommodations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#accessibility-and-accommodations\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>If you have approved accommodations, please request your accommodation letter and contact me early so we can make arrangements in time.\nIf you think you may need accommodations but have not yet set them up, the <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://cea.uark.edu/\">Center for Educational Access</a> can help. Temporary conditions can affect access too, so please reach out promptly when they arise.</p>", "a[href=\"#letter-grades\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Letter grades<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#letter-grades\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>Here is the tentative grade distribution.\nIt is <strong>just a reference</strong>, and I will let you know if it needs to change during the course.</p>", "a[href=\"assignments/index.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Assignments<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#assignments\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h1><h2>Published homework<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#published-homework\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#attendance-and-participation\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Attendance and participation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#attendance-and-participation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>Attendance is not graded, and there is no absence penalty.\nIf you need to miss class, you can use the posted notes, online questions, homework, and other resources to keep up independently.</p><p>Please keep track of course material, announcements, deadlines, and assessments.\nIf your online work, homework, or exams suggest that your current study routine is not serving you, I may reach out with ideas such as regular attendance or office hours.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link", "no-hover-preview"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(`article.bd-article ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 500, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
